Interpretation and limits:
- The historical bag directly records a discontinuous /odom_incremental step immediately after a mapping correction and shows the matching /odom step. The replay reproduces /odom from the TransformFusion formula; the selected large-jump events have machine-precision residuals. The larger all-sample maximum residual is retained because recorder arrival order is not exact callback ordering.
- The source queue is pruned only by header stamp <= latest mapping header; queue entries newer than that anchor remain. The selected events directly bracket a retained front receipt before the mapping correction and a back receipt after it. Calling these samples old/new epochs is still an inference because the messages have no epoch tag and recorder order is not executor callback order.
- This is same-system historical corroboration, not a frame-by-frame observation of the 11:13 failure: that bag omitted /odom_incremental, and the historical binary may differ from the current uncommitted checkout. Recorder arrival order is not exact executor scheduling.
